    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nMy project had a build system that worked fine on cython 3.2.5 and earlier, based on [Compiling shared module using setuptools](https://cython.readthedocs.io/en/latest/src/userguide/source_files_and_compilation.html#compiling-shared-module-using-setuptools).\n\nHowever following 3.2.6 (possibly #7723) the build fails **on the first try** with the following error and then **succeeds on the second**:\n\n```\n    with Utils.open_source_file(source_filename) as f:\n         ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"Cython/Utils.py\", line 418, in Cython.Utils.open_source_file\nFileNotFoundError: build/build/_cyutility.pyx\n```\n\nTo get to \"first time\" again, I just rm all files in build directory.\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n```bash\npython setup.py build_ext --inplace\n```\n\nBuild system **setup.py** looks roughly like this, though tried changing the order and presense and location of pretty much everything without finding a workaround (except for the obvious one: run the build twice).\n\n```python\nfrom Cython.Compiler import Options\nOptions.annotate = True\nsharedCythonModule = True\n\n#...\n\nif sharedCythonModule:\n    extensions = [Extension(\"_cyutility\",\n                            extra_link_args=extra_link_args,\n                            sources=[\"_cyutility.c\"])]\nelse:\n    extensions = []\n\nfor directoryx in [\"*\"]:\n    extensions.append(\n        Extension(directoryx, [directoryx + \".pyx\"],\n                  extra_compile_args=extra_compile_args,\n                  extra_link_args=extra_link_args,\n                  libraries=libraries,\n                  include_dirs=include_dirs,\n                  runtime_library_dirs=library_dirs,\n                  library_dirs=library_dirs,\n                  define_macros=[('CYTHON_TRACE', str(profile))],\n              )\n        )\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    args = {'nthreads': (cpu_count()+1)//2,\n            'build_dir': 'build',\n            'language_level': 3}\n    if sharedCythonModule:\n        args['shared_utility_qualified_name'] = '_cyutility'\n\n    setup(\n        ext_modules = cythonize(extensions, **args)\n    )\n```\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\nShould build without error first time like on 3.2.5\n\n### OS\n\nLinux\n\n### Python version\n\n3.13\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.3.0\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_",
